  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given two undirected binary trees T1T_1T1​ and T2T_2T2​ , check if the second tree T2T_2T2​ exists as a **subtree** in the first tree T1T_1T1​.\n\nA **binary tree** is a tree in which each node has at most two children.\n\nA **subtree** of a node xxx in a tree TTT is a tree consisting of the node xxx and all of its **descendants** in TTT. A **descendant** of a node xxx is any node reachable from it by repeated proceeding from a parent to its child.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains two space separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of nodes in the two binary trees.\nNext N−1N - 1N−1 lines contain three space separated characters p1i,c1i,Rip1_i, c1_i, R_ip1i​,c1i​,Ri​, describing the first tree with edge informations - p1ip1_ip1i​ is an integer denoting the parent node of the iiith edge, c1ic1_ic1i​ is child node, and the letter RiR_iRi​ denotes whether the child is left child or right child, it's value is `L` if c1ic1_ic1i​ is left child of p1ip1_ip1i​, else `R`.\nSimilarly, next M−1M - 1M−1 lines contain three space separated characters p2i,c2i,Rip2_i, c2_i, R_ip2i​,c2i​,Ri​, describing the second tree with edge informations - p2ip2_ip2i​ is an integer denoting the parent node of the iiith edge, c2ic2_ic2i​ is child node, and the letter RiR_iRi​ denotes whether the child is left child or right child, it's value is `L` if c2ic2_ic2i​ is left child of p2ip2_ip2i​, else `R`.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nComplete the given function whic should return a single integer 111 if the binary tree T2T_2T2​ exists as a subtree in the binary tree T1T_1T1​ and 000 otherwise.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,M≤10001 \\leq N, M \\leq 10001≤N,M≤1000",
      "1≤p1i,p2i,c1i,c2i≤100001 \\leq p1_i, p2_i, c1_i, c2_i \\leq 100001≤p1i​,p2i​,c1i​,c2i​≤10000",
      "RiR_iRi​ = `L` or `R`",
      "All pip_ipi​'s and cic_ici​'s are distinct."
    ],
